## 💡 Key Takeaways

- **Teams** are top-level containers; **Channels** organize conversations
- **Private channels** restrict access to specific members
- **Guest access** must be enabled at org level before guests can join
- **Team creation policies** prevent Teams sprawl
- **Multiple owners** ensure continuity if one leaves

---

## 🔗 Team vs Channel Structure

| Concept | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Team | Top-level container |
| Standard Channel | Accessible to all members |
| Private Channel | Restricted to specific members |
| Shared Channel | Accessible to external users |
